hessalonica falls.","m":12,"cp":"kingdom-of-thessalonica","cpn":"Kingdom of Thessalonica","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas","c":3},{"y":1225,"t":"gain","x":"Spring 1225: Theodore overruns Latin Thrace.","cp":"latin-empire","cpn":"Latin Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas","c":2},{"y":1225,"t":"gain","x":"1225: Adrianople taken from the Nicaean garrison.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":3},{"y":1227,"t":"rename","x":"1227: Theodore is crowned emperor at Thessalonica; the Epirote state is styled the Empire of Thessalonica.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas","c":2},{"y":1227,"t":"capital_move","x":"1227: the court sits at Thessalonica (infobox 'Thessalonica (1227-1230)').","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":2},{"y":1230,"t":"split","x":"1230: the realm divides.","cp":"empire-of-thessalonica","cpn":"Empire of Thessalonica","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Klokotnitsa","c":2},{"y":1230,"t":"capital_move","x":"c. 1230/31: Michael II rules Epirus from Arta again.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":2},{"y":1230,"t":"loss","x":"9 March 1230: Klokotnitsa.","m":3,"cp":"second-bulgarian-empire","cpn":"Second Bulgarian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Klokotnitsa","c":3},{"y":1236,"t":"gain","x":"By 1236: Michael II holds Corfu.","cp":"empire-of-thessalonica","cpn":"Empire of Thessalonica","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","c":1},{"y":1241,"t":"gain","x":"1241: Thessaly to Michael II.","cp":"empire-of-thessalonica","cpn":"Empire of Thessalonica","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","c":3},{"y":1246,"t":"gain","x":"1246: Michael II expands as Bulgaria crumbles.","cp":"second-bulgarian-empire","cpn":"Second Bulgarian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","c":1},{"y":1252,"t":"loss","x":"1252: the treaty of Larissa.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","c":3},{"y":1256,"t":"loss","x":"1256: Dyrrhachium and Servia to Nicaea.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_II_Laskaris","c":3},{"y":1257,"t":"gain","x":"1257: Michael II revolts.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_II_Laskaris","c":3},{"y":1258,"t":"loss","x":"1258: Manfred of Sicily takes the Epirote share of the Albanian coast.","cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia","c":2},{"y":1259,"t":"loss","x":"1259: Corfu to Manfred as Helena's dowry.","cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corfu","c":3},{"y":1259,"t":"loss","x":"Spring 1259: Ohrid and Deavolis to Nicaea.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia","c":3},{"y":1259,"t":"loss","x":"1259: Prilep back to Nicaea, bridging a silence.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia","c":1},{"y":1259,"t":"occupation_start","x":"Summer 1259: Pelagonia.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia","c":2},{"y":1260,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1260: Michael II recovers his domains.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia","c":2},{"y":1268,"t":"split","x":"1267/68: the partition between Michael II's sons.","cp":"thessaly","cpn":"Thessaly","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","c":3},{"y":1278,"t":"gain","x":"1278: Butrint retaken from the Byzantines.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butrint","c":3},{"y":1279,"t":"loss",