sicily","cpn":"House of Anjou-Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_VI_of_Brienne","c":2},{"y":1332,"t":"gain","x":"1332: John II invades Thessaly.","cp":"thessaly","cpn":"Thessaly","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II_Orsini","c":2},{"y":1336,"t":"loss","x":"1335-1336: Andronikos III closes in.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_II_Orsini","c":2},{"y":1337,"t":"loss","x":"1337: the Byzantine annexation.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":3},{"y":1339,"t":"gain","x":"Late 1338-1339: the Arta rebellion.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_II_Orsini","c":2},{"y":1340,"t":"loss","x":"1340: the revolt collapses.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Monomachos","c":3},{"y":1356,"t":"gain","x":"Spring 1356: Nikephoros II restores the despotate.","cp":"serbian-empire","cpn":"Serbian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_II_Orsini","c":2},{"y":1359,"t":"loss","x":"1359: Achelous.","cp":"serbian-empire","cpn":"Serbian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medieval_Thessaly","c":3},{"y":1359,"t":"loss","x":"1359: Epirus to the Albanian clans.","cp":"despotate-of-arta","cpn":"Despotate of Arta","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Achelous_(1359)","c":2},{"y":1359,"t":"loss","x":"1359: Ioannina submits to Simeon Uros.","cp":"serbian-empire","cpn":"Serbian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Achelous_(1359)","c":2},{"y":1367,"t":"gain","x":"1367: the Despotate of Ioannina.","cp":"serbian-empire","cpn":"Serbian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Preljubovi%C4%87","c":2},{"y":1380,"t":"gain","x":"1380-1381: Thomas on the offensive with Ottoman help.","cp":"albanian-principalities","cpn":"Albanian principalities","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Preljubovi%C4%87","c":2},{"y":1385,"t":"rename","x":"February 1385: Esau de' Buondelmonti.","m":2,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esau_de%27_Buondelmonti","c":3},{"y":1399,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1399: Esau captured.","cp":"albanian-principalities","cpn":"Albanian principalities","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esau_de%27_Buondelmonti","c":2},{"y":1400,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1400: Esau returns to Ioannina.","cp":"albanian-principalities","cpn":"Albanian principalities","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esau_de%27_Buondelmonti","c":1},{"y":1411,"t":"rename","x":"February 1411: the Tocco despotate.","m":2,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_I_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1411,"t":"merge","x":"1411: the Tocco islands and Ioannina united under one ruler.","m":2,"cp":"house-of-tocco","cpn":"County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos (Tocco)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_I_Tocco","c":2},{"y":1416,"t":"gain","x":"4 October 1416: Arta surrenders.","m":10,"cp":"despotate-of-arta","cpn":"Despotate of Arta","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_I_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1421,"t":"gain","x":"1421: Glarentza bought.","cp":"Oliverio Franco","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glarentza","c":2},{"y":1428,"t":"loss","x":"1 May 1428: Glarentza handed to Constantine Palaiologos.","m":5,"cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_XI_Palaiologos","c":3},{"y":1430,"t":"loss","x":"9 October 1430: Ioannina surrenders to the Ottomans ('obtained the surrender of the city on October 9, 1430').","m":10,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_II_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1430,"t":"capital_move","x":"October 1430: the court moves to Arta.","m":10,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_II_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1449,"t":"loss","x":"24 March 1449: Arta falls.","m":3,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_III_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1449,"t":"capital_move","x":"1449: the court moves to Angelokastron (infobox 'Angelokastron (1449-60)').","m":3,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":2},{"y":1460,"t":"loss","x":"1460: Angelokastron lost.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_III_Tocco","c":2},{"y":1460,"t":"capital_move","x":"1460: Vonitsa, the last mainland seat (infobox 'Vonitsa (1460-1479)'); Leonardo ruled from Lefkada.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":2},{"y":1479,"t":"loss","x":"August-September 1479: the end.","m":9,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_III_Tocco","c":3},{"y":1479,"t":"dissolve","x":"1479: the Despotate of Epirus ends with the Ottoman capture of Vonitsa.","m":9,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Epirote conquest of Thessaly and Thessalonica","from":1212,"to":1224,"outcome":"Epirote victory: Michael I took Thessaly in 1212; Theodore 'gradually conquered all of Thessalonica except the city itself' over nine years and took the city in December 1224; Peter of Courtenay captured 1217.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas"},{"name":"Theodore's Thracian campaign","from":1225,"to":1226,"outcome":"Theodore took western Thrace from the Latins and Adrianople from the Nicaeans; 'Constantinople itself was not attacked'; a truce with the Latins in 1228.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas"},{"name":"Battle of Klokotnitsa","from":1230,"to":1230,"outcome":"Bulgarian victory on 9 March 1230; Theodore captured and blinded; Thrace, most of Macedonia and Albania Bulgarian; Thessalonica a Bulgarian vassal under Manuel; Epirus proper independent under Michael II.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Klokotnitsa"},{"name":"Epirote-Nicaean war of 1251-1253","from":1251,"to":1253,"outcome":"Nicaean victory: the treaty of Larissa (1252) ceded all Epirote holdings in Macedonia and put Kruja under Nicaean suzerainty; Vodena, Kastoria and Deabolis taken in winter 1252/53.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas"},{"name":"Epirote-Nicaean conflict (1257-1259) and the Battle of Pelagonia","from":1257,"to":1260,"outcome":"Nicaean victory at Pelagonia (summer or autumn 1259): 'Collapse of the Epiroto-Latin League'; Arta taken and Ioannina besieged, then 'the Nicaean successes were largely undone' in 1260; Manfred kept Corfu and Albania; Michael II accepted Michael VIII's…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pelagonia"},{"name":"Angevin-Byzantine war in Albania","from":1272,"to":1281,"outcome":"Charles of Anjou took Dyrrhachium in 1272; the Byzantine campaign of 1274 (Byzantine forces re-entered Butrint) 'infringed on Nikephoros' interests' and he allied with Charles in 1276; the coalition of Charles, Nikephoros and John I Doukas drove the…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_I_Komnenos_Doukas"},{"name":"Angevin-Epirote war of 1304-1307","from":1304,"to":1307,"outcome":"Epirus recovered Butrint and Naupaktos in 1304-1305; the Angevin invasion of 1307 'ended with a compromise' returning many fortresses to Philip of Taranto, who gave up his claim in 1312.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_I_Komnenos_Doukas"},{"name":"Byzantine annexation of Epirus","from":1336,"to":1340,"outcome":"Byzantine victory: Epirus annexed 1337/1338; the Arta revolt of late 1338 crushed by the end of 1340 ('the various rebel-held strongholds capitulated'); John Angelos governor.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Monomachos"},{"name":"Battle of Achelous (1359)","from":1358,"to":1359,"outcome":"Albanian victory; Nikephoros II killed; 'Albanians take control over Epirus, except Ioannina'; Despotate of Arta re-established; Thessaly to Simeon Uros.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Achelous_(1359)"},{"name":"Albanian-Epirote wars of Ioannina","from":1367,"to":1416,"outcome":"Thomas Preljubovic (with Ottoman help from 1380) and Esau held Ioannina against Losha and the Shpata; Esau was captured by Zenebishi in 1399; Carlo I Tocco 'finally managed to subdue the Albanian clans and seized Arta in 1416'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Arta"},{"name":"Tocco-Byzantine war in the Morea","from":1426,"to":1428,"outcome":"Byzantine victory at the Echinades (1427), 'the last in the Empire's naval history'; Glarentza and the Moreot lands handed over as Maddalena Tocco's dowry on 1 May 1428.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Echinades_(1427)"},{"name":"Ottoman conquest of the Tocco despotate","from":1430,"to":1479,"outcome":"Ottoman conquest in stages: Ioannina 1430, Arta and the mainland 1449, Angelokastro 1460, Vonitsa and the Ionian islands 1479; Leonardo III fled to Taranto.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_III_Tocco"}],"certainty":[{"from":1205,"to":1479,"level":"soft","note":"Medieval Balkan frontiers held by towns and castles; no treaty line is recorded except the 1252 Larissa treaty's cession of named towns."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Epirus","title":"Despotate of Epirus"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_I_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Michael I Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Theodore Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Michael II Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_I_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Nikephoros I Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_I_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Thomas I Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas_Orsini","title":"Nicholas Orsini"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II_Orsini","title":"John II Orsini"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikephoros_II_Orsini","title":"Nikephoros II Orsini"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Kl